1
00:36:15,763 --> 00:36:19,836
You ask him now, his number is Summit...

2
00:36:19,866 --> 00:36:23,986
- Summit 7537.
- Thank you Lizzie.

3
00:36:24,183 --> 00:36:26,687
- Summit...?
- 7537.

4
00:36:30,323 --> 00:36:33,100
Not bad, eh Andy? That means new business.

5
00:36:35,097 --> 00:36:37,822
Now, you see? Somebody
wants to buy a house.

6
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:42,197
- Mark Fleming speaking.
- Oh hello Dale.

7
00:36:45,004 --> 00:36:47,282
Well, hang on a minute
honey while I see if I have them.

8
00:36:48,067 --> 00:36:49,726
It's Dale Bailey all excited.

9
00:36:49,756 --> 00:36:53,453
Miss Van Gorder wants to know
if I have the floor plans of the Oaks.

10
00:36:53,830 --> 00:36:55,852
Now, what would she want
with the floor plans?

11
00:36:56,712 --> 00:37:00,665
Well, she suggested to me that your
uncle might've hidden the bank loot there.

12
00:37:01,269 --> 00:37:02,540
Are the plans here?

13
00:37:04,710 --> 00:37:06,777
Somewhere in the house itself.

14
00:37:08,904 --> 00:37:11,801
Wait a minute, there is a place where
uncle Johnny might've kept those blueprints.

15
00:37:12,963 --> 00:37:13,676
What place?

16
00:37:13,706 --> 00:37:16,041
Well, I heard him talk
about it a good many years ago.

17
00:37:16,071 --> 00:37:18,491
I can't be sure of the exact location.

18
00:37:19,697 --> 00:37:22,501
Anyway, I don't think the old boy
had the guts to steal a million.

19
00:37:22,983 --> 00:37:25,892
But if I find those plans,
I'll let you know Andy.

20
00:37:26,962 --> 00:37:28,048
Hello Dale?

21
00:37:28,349 --> 00:37:31,123
Look honey, I haven't seen
those plans since I was a kid.

22
00:37:31,153 --> 00:37:33,249
But I'll come over tonight,
and maybe we can find them.

23
00:37:34,214 --> 00:37:36,189
Thank you Mark, we'll expect you.

24
00:37:38,570 --> 00:37:40,922
He seems to think they're
here in the house somewhere.

25
00:37:40,952 --> 00:37:43,470
- He's coming over tonight.
- Oh, that's good.

26
00:37:43,893 --> 00:37:46,350
Dale and Judie are my
house guests for the weekend.

27
00:37:46,576 --> 00:37:48,682
Would you like to have
dinner with us tonight?

28
00:37:48,712 --> 00:37:51,928
Oh no thank you, I couldn't,
I still have a few calls to make.

29
00:37:52,546 --> 00:37:56,407
You know, if Judy's testimony is
going to clear Vick Bailey and implicate...

30
00:37:56,437 --> 00:38:00,718
John Fleming, others may get the idea
that there's buried treasure in this house.

31
00:38:01,065 --> 00:38:04,758
Don't even mention your testimony
until you're actually on the stand.

32
00:38:04,788 --> 00:38:05,768
Oh, I won't.

33
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:08,856
That's a smart girl
Judie and a very lovely girl.

34
00:38:09,066 --> 00:38:10,397
- Well, good afternoon ladies.
- Doctor.

35
00:38:10,427 --> 00:38:11,919
- Doctor.
- Goodbye Dr. Wells.

36
00:38:11,949 --> 00:38:13,653
Come on girls, let's go.

37
00:38:57,641 --> 00:39:01,756
So many unusual things
have happened here this summer.

38
00:39:02,088 --> 00:39:04,108
The more I think about it...

39
00:39:05,119 --> 00:39:08,737
the more I realize I should've
be putting them down on paper.

40
00:39:09,822 --> 00:39:12,822
Weren't you your husband's secretary Dale?

41
00:39:12,852 --> 00:39:15,174
- Yes, I was.
- You take shorthand?

42
00:39:16,455 --> 00:39:19,772
Well my dear, if you'd like
to have your mind occupied...

43
00:39:20,661 --> 00:39:25,499
I want you to work with me while I write
the story of this fantastic criminal...

44
00:39:26,630 --> 00:39:27,911
the Bat.

45
00:40:16,137 --> 00:40:18,353
- Wonderful dinner.
- Thank you.

46
00:40:19,190 --> 00:40:20,336
Was really nice.

47
00:40:21,693 --> 00:40:22,823
Was a good dinner Lizzie.

48
00:40:22,853 --> 00:40:24,225
- As usual.
- Wonderful.

49
00:40:25,733 --> 00:40:28,944
Oh, what a lovely piece of silver.

50
00:40:29,155 --> 00:40:34,160
- It's an original, isn't it?
- Yes, they still use them in England.
